Reaffirming the right of all States to self-defence in accordance with Article 51 of the Charter of the United Nations and in accordance with international humanitarian law,
Stressing the need to prevent the conflict from spreading, and the importance of a two-State solution,
Welcoming the diplomatic efforts of the Secretary-General, regional leaders, and all those working to secure the release of hostages and to provide humanitarian assistance,
